From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:06:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Suggest the same model on a subscription with more room
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The stats line shows a chip such as 'Opus 5.5 on Claude Personal →' when
the current subscription is on pace to run out before its 5h or weekly
window resets (or is 90% used), naming the signed-in subscription with
the most headroom that offers the same model. It also suggests another
subscription whose weekly allowance resets within a day mostly unused.
Model-scoped weeklies only count for their own model family. Clicking
switches the thread through the usual model selection; the tooltip
explains why and when a started thread cannot switch.
